  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">The Martyrdom of Polycarp, written by the church at Smyrna around 155-160, is the oldest surviving account of a Christian martyrdom outside the New Testament. Polycarp, aged 86, refuses to swear by Caesar’s fortune or revile Christ. The account is theological as much as historical: the church at Smyrna reads his death as a liturgical act patterned on the passion of Christ, right down to the timing and the prayer.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
    
